  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 6.2. Increased capacity of Member States to strengthen policies and strategies to promote and ensure equal opportunities, participation and treatment between women and men, including equal remuneration for work of equal value</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government of Saudi Arabia adopted the national policy to promote equality and non-discrimination in employment and occupation in Saudi Arabia in January 2023. The policy includes a set of goals and measures to prevent discrimination and promote equal opportunity in employment and occupations and enable groups with less opportunities to join and remain in the labour market.

The policy aims to develop a legal and policy framework that explicitly defines and prevents discrimination and promotes equality and inclusion while at the same time promoting the participation of women and disadvantaged groups in the labour force. Specific measures include supporting gender-responsive law reforms, reviewing legislations aimed at promoting non-discrimination (this includes social security legislation, maternity protection and flexible work, amongst others); supporting school to work transitions for women and disadvantaged groups and implementing return to work programmes for women, amongst others.
 With the support from the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, the ILO supported the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Development in drafting the Policy on Equality in Employment and Occupations by developing and building on the results of a legal framework review and an inclusive labour market analysis, which were prepared by the ILO in previous biennia.</narrative>
   </description>
